---
---

<section id="methodology" class="py-20 border-b border-slate-800/60 bg-[#080C14]">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-16">
      <div class="inline-block text-xs font-mono font-semibold tracking-wider text-emerald-400 uppercase bg-emerald-950/40 px-3 py-1 rounded-md border border-emerald-800/40 mb-3">
        Research Methodology
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
        The 5 Invariants of Causal Research
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        Over 90% of quantitative strategies fail when deployed live because academic backtests rely on unrealistic assumptions. 
        In our lab, every research experiment must satisfy five non-negotiable invariants before capital consideration.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <!-- Invariant 1 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
          01
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Strict Temporal Causality</h3>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-400">t_available &le; t_decision</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          No strategy can observe a price, candle close, or indicator until its broadcast timestamp has elapsed in real time. We strictly reject synthetic or forward-looking price arrays.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Invariant 2 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
          02
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Purged & Embargoed Cross-Validation</h3>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-400">Lopez de Prado Protocol</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Financial time-series possess long-memory serial autocorrelation. Standard k-fold cross-validation leaks information. We enforce temporal purge windows and post-trade embargoes between splits.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Invariant 3 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
          03
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Exact Double-Entry Accounting</h3>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400">Zero Floating-Point Drift</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          `float` arithmetic silently introduces compounding rounding errors over millions of simulated trades. Every fill, balance debit, and fee deduction is recorded using fixed-scale `Decimal` double-entry ledgering.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Invariant 4 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
          04
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Frictional Reality & Fee Hurdle</h3>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400">Maker/Taker & Queue Delay</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Mid-price fills are an illusion. Orders are matched against real simulated book depth, factoring in maker rebates, taker penalties, queue priorities, and market impact slippage curves.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Invariant 5 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors">
        <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
          05
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Out-of-Sample Lockbox</h3>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-teal-400">Anti-P-Hacking Protocol</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Tuning parameters until a curve looks pretty guarantees overfitting. Final model performance is verified once and once only on a cryptographically sealed lockbox partition of unseen market history.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Invariant 6 / Philosophy -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 to-slate-900/40 border border-cyan-900/40 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-teal-500/10 border border-teal-500/20 text-teal-400 font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            &infin;
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-100 font-mono">Reproducible Provenance</h3>
          <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-mono text-teal-400">Git Commit &times; Data Hash</div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Every backtest result records the exact commit hash, raw dataset SHA-256 fingerprint, seed, and environment dependencies for total determinism.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
